&Q000391 = A šir-namšub to Nanna for Ur-Namma (Ur-Namma F)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.4.1.6
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.4.1.6&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. [ur₃]-bad₃ kug-ga-ta hi-li gur₃-ru
#tr.en: Imbued with allure from the shining rooftops, @wSN{Urim},
#lem: urbad[rooftop]; kug[pure]; hili[attractiveness]; gur[lift]
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. urim₂#{ki} uš-u₂-zu he₂-ŋal₂ ki us₂-sa
#tr.en: your foundation rests on abundance. City, your lord rides high in joy,
#lem: Urim[1]SN; uš[foundation]; heŋal[plenty]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. asil₃-la₂-a %e uru₂ %e u₃-mu-un-zu %s he₂-a-u₅!
#tr.en: @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}} rides high indeed;
#lem: asilala[joy]; uru[city]; umun[lord]N; u[ride]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. {d}ur-{d}namma he₂-a-u₅!
#tr.en: the one adorned with a lapis-lazuli beard rides high indeed!
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; u[ride]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. sun₄ za-gin₃ sud₄-sud₄ he₂-a-u₅!
#tr.en: He is the tallest among all the lords,
#lem: sum[beard]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; sud[distant]; u[ride]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. gu₂-en-ta en sukud-da ed₂-de₃-bi-ta nir-ŋal₂
#tr.en: appearing as the noblest among them.
#lem: guʾen[assembly room]; en[lord]; sukud[height]; e[leave]; nirŋal[authoritative]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. abula-zu e₃-<a> a mah gaba-šu-ŋar nu-tuku
#tr.en: Those who leave through your gate are an uncontrollable flood. Shrine @wSN{Urim},
#lem: abula[gate]; e[leave]; a[water]; mah[great]; gabašuŋar[rival]; tuku[acquire]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. eš₃ urim₂{ki} šag₄-zu kur he₂-ŋal₂ bar-zu hur-saŋ# he-<nun-na>
#tr.en: your interior is a mountain of abundance, your exterior a hill of plenty.
#lem: eš[shrine]; Urim[1]SN; šag[heart]; kur[mountain(s)]; heŋal[plenty]; bar[outside]; hursaŋ[mountain]; henun[plenty]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. e₂-kiš-nu-ŋal₂ hur-saŋ galam-ma šag₄-bi lu₂ nu-zu
#tr.en: No one can learn the interior of the @wTN{E-kiš-nu-ŋal}, the artfully fashioned hill.
#lem: Ekišnuŋal[1]TN; hursaŋ[mountain]; galam[skilful]; šag[heart]; lu[person]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. e₂-zu! kur gi-rin-na mu-zu šag₄ gur-ra
#tr.en: Your temple is a shimmering mountain; your very name is merciful.
#lem: e[house]; kur[mountain(s)]; girim[flower]; mu[name]; šag[heart]; gur[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. en-zu en sig₇-ga mu pad₃-da
#tr.en: Your lord is the one called as the beautiful lord, the child of @wDN{Ninsumun},
#lem: en[lord]; en[lord]; sissig[green-yellow]; mu[name]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. dumu {d}nin-sumun₂ me-te kur-kur-ra
#tr.en: the ornament of all the lands.
#lem: dumu[child]; Ninsumunak[1]DN; mete[appropriate thing]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. e₂ me gal-zu rab₃ diŋir-re-e-ne kalam-ma la₂-am₃
#tr.en: House, your great divine power is the shackle of the gods put on the Land.
#lem: e[house]; me[Being]; galanzu[wise]; raba[clamp]; diŋir[deity]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. kan₄-zu diŋir-zu diŋir sig₇-ga mu pad₃-da
#tr.en: Your gate is named by your god, the beautiful god; only when it is is open does @wDN{Utu} illuminate from the horizon.
#lem: kan[gate]; diŋir[deity]; diŋir[deity]; sissig[green-yellow]; mu[name]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. ŋal₂ da₁₃-da₁₃-bi!(GA) {d}utu an-ur₂-ta ud mi-ni-in-ŋar-ra
#tr.en: Your platform, the place where the fates are determined by the gods, in order to make just decisions,
#lem: ŋal[open]; taka[set aside]; Utu[1]DN; anur[horizon]; ud[storm]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. gi#-sa₂-zu ki nam tar-ra diŋir-re-e-ne di si sa₂ ku₅-ru-de₃
#tr.en: is where the @wDN{Anuna},
#lem: kisa[platform]; ki[place]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; diŋir[deity]; did[lawsuit]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; kud[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. {[d]}[a]-nun#-na diŋir an ki-ka ad mi-ni-in-gi-gi-ne
#tr.en: the gods of heaven and earth, take counsel.
#lem: Anunak[1]DN; diŋir[deity]; an[sky]; ki[place]; ad[voice]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. [...] X-zu-ta munus zid giri₁₇-zal a-a gu₂ peš-a
#tr.en: Your …… makes (?) the faithful woman joyous, the father proud.
#lem: X; X; munus[woman]; zid[right]; kirizal[joy]; aya[father]; gu[neck]; peš[thick]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. [šag₄-ga-zu-ta] ŋiš-hur kug-ga-a hul-ŋal₂ [nu]-mu#-[un]-dab₅!-be₂
#tr.en: In your interior the evildoer dare not lay hold of the holy statutes.
#lem: šag[heart]; ŋešhur[plan]; kug[pure]; huluŋal[evil]; dab[seize]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. [e₂ gi]-gun₄#-na ninda-ba-bi ki-bal kuš₇ [su₃-su₃]
#tr.en: House whose offerings of the temple terrace devastate the rebel lands.
#lem: e[house]; giguna[high sacred terrace]; nindaba[ration]; kibala[rebel land]; kuš[devastation]; su[sprinkle]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. [dub-la₂]-mah# ki nam tar-re-za
#tr.en: At your @wTN{Dubla-maḫ}, the place where the fates are determined,
#lem: Dublamah[1]TN; ki[place]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. [diŋir] gal#-gal-e-ne nam mi-ni-tar-re-ne
#tr.en: the great gods determine the fates. @wDN{Suen} chose @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad},
#lem: diŋir[deity]; gal[big]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. ki-en-gi ki-uri uŋ₃ saŋ gig₂-ga
#tr.en: the black-headed people,
#lem: Kengir[1]; Akkad[1 Akkad]; uŋ[people]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. {d}ur-{d}namma {d}suen šag₄-ge ba-ni-in-pad₃
#tr.en: and @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}} in his heart.
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; Suen[1]DN; šag[heart]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. lugal hi-li gur₃-ru me-lem₄ kalam-ma dul-la
#tr.en: Let me give praise to the king endowed with allure,
#lem: lugal[king]; hili[attractiveness]; gur[lift]; melim[frightening splendor]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; dul[cover]
#etcsl: line-id=25

#etcsl#cite Cited in Ur III catalogue at Yale, 0.1.2, line 17; OB catalogue from Nibru (N6), 0.2.13, line 12

26. %e me-e {en}u₃-mu-un-ra %s mi₂ zid-de₃-eš
#tr.en: the radiance covering the nation, Lord @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}! In his heart @wDN{Ašimbabbar} has chosen @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}},
#lem: meʾe[I]IP; umun[lord]N; mi[cvne]; zid[right]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. {d}ur-{d}namma ga-an-i-i-de₃
#tr.en: @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}} who is endowed with allure,
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; e[bring out]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. {d}ur-{d}namma hi-li gur₃-ru me-lem₄ kalam-ma dul-la
#tr.en: the radiance covering the nation,
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; hili[attractiveness]; gur[lift]; melim[frightening splendor]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; dul[cover]
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. {d}ur-{d}namma {d}dil-im₂-babbar šag₄-ge ba-ni-in-pad₃
#tr.en: placing thereby a shackle on all the lands and blocking the way with a strong bolt.
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; Dilimbabbar[1]DN; šag[heart]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. {ŋiš}rab₃-ba kur-kur-ra im-mi-in-ŋar
#tr.en: The king is worthy of @wDN{Suen}!
#lem: raba[clamp]; kur[mountain(s)]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. si-ŋar kalag-ga im-mi-in-gib-ba lugal {d}suen-ra tum₂-ma-am₃
#tr.en: Wickedness cannot pass unnoticed before his eyes.
#lem: siŋar[bolt]; kalag[strong]; gilim[cross]; lugal[king]; Suen[1]DN; tum[suitable]
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. niŋ₂-erim₂ igi-ni-še₃ nu-dib₂-be₂
#tr.en: @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}} has accomplished an achievement, justice!
#lem: niŋerim[evil]; igi[eye]; dib[pass]
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. niŋ₂-si-sa₂ {d}ur-{d}namma niŋ₂-gur₁₁ sa₂ bi₂-in-dug₄
#tr.en: He fills the wicked land with his battle-cry.
#lem: niŋsisa[justice]; Urnamma[1]RN; niŋgur[property]; sa[equal]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. za-pa-aŋ₂-ŋa₂-ni-še₃ kur erim₂-ma bi₂-in-ŋar
#tr.en: The rebellious land is overthrown,
#lem: zipaŋ[voice]; kur[mountain(s)]; erim[enemy]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. ki-bal-bi mu-un-sig₁₀ {d}ur-{d}namma maškim im-me
#tr.en: @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}} acts (?) as the constable.
#lem: kibala[rebel land]; sig[put into]; Urnamma[1]RN; maškim[an administrator]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. lugal-e e₂ {d}suen-na-ke₄
#tr.en: She has determined a fate for the king and the temple of @wDN{Suen},
#lem: lugal[king]; e[house]; Suen[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. {id₂}idigna {id₂}buranuna {d}ur-<{d}>namma-ke₄ nam mu-ni-ib₂-<<BI>>-tar-re!
#tr.en: for the @wWN{Tigris} and the @wWN{Euphrates} and for @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}.
#lem: Idigna[1 Tigris]; Buranun[1 Euphrates]; Urnamma[1]RN; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. {[d]}utu# an-ur₂-ta e₃-a-ba
#tr.en: As the sun rises from the horizon, may the population multiply!
#lem: Utu[1]DN; anur[horizon]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. [nam]-lu₂#-ulu₃ hu-mu-ši-ib₂-daŋal-e-ne
#tr.en: May he pass the …… of @wDN{Ninsumun}!
#lem: namlulu[humanity]; daŋal[wide]
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. [...] {[d]}nin-sumun₂-ka hu-mu-ni-in-dib₂-dib₂-be₂ u₆ di X X
#tr.en: …… admiration. Its lady, the lady who loves possessions,
#lem: X; Ninsumunak[1]DN; dib[pass]; u[admiration]; di[speak]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. [nin]-bi# nin niŋ₂-gur₁₁-e ki aŋ₂
#tr.en: who loves him, has determined a fate for @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}};
#lem: nin[lady]; nin[lady]; niŋgur[property]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. [ki] aŋ₂#-ŋa₂-na-ke₄ {d}ur-{d}namma-ke₄ nam mu-ni-ib-tar-re
#tr.en: @wDN{Ningal}, its lady, the lady who loves possessions,
#lem: ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; Urnamma[1]RN; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. {[d]}nin#-gal nin-bi nin niŋ₂-gur₁₁-e ki aŋ₂
#tr.en: the woman of princely seed,
#lem: Ningal[1]DN; nin[lady]; nin[lady]; niŋgur[property]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. [munus a] nun-na-ke₄ {d}ur-{d}namma-ke₄ <<niŋ₂-gur₁₁-e-ki-aŋ₂>> nam mu-ni-ib-tar-re
#tr.en: has determined a fate for @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}.
#lem: munus[woman]; a[water]; nun[prince]; Urnamma[1]RN; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. sipad# {d}ur-{d}namma-ke₄ il₂ e₂ {d}suen-na-še₃ sun₄ za-gin₃ sud₄-sud₄
#tr.en: The shepherd @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}} is elevated; in the house of @wDN{Suen},
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; Urnamma[1]RN; il[raise]; e[house]; Suen[1]DN; sum[beard]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. [...] {d}nin-X hu-mu-ni-ib-dib₂-dib₂-be₂
#tr.en: he is the one adorned with a lapis lazuli beard.
#lem: X; Nin.X[0]DN; dib[pass]
#etcsl: line-id=46

47. [...] X dug₃-ga-am₃ hi-li-ba ku₇-ku₇-dam <<nu>>
#tr.en: May he pass ……! …… is good,
#lem: X; X; dug[good]; hili[attractiveness]; kud[sweet]
#etcsl: line-id=47

48. {[d]}nin#-lil₂-le ud-da u₃-tud-da-gin₇
#tr.en: is sweet in its luxuriance. Like @wDN{Ninlil} who gives birth in a storm,
#lem: Ninlil[1]DN; ud[storm]; utud[give birth (to)]
#etcsl: line-id=48

49. [dumu] {[d]}nin#-sumun₂-na-ke₄ za-e hu-mu-ra-u₃-tud
#tr.en: child of @wDN{Ninsumun}, she has given birth to you.
#lem: dumu[child]; Ninsumunak[1]DN; zaʾe[you]; utud[give birth (to)]
#etcsl: line-id=49

50. sipad-da an kug-ga hu-mu#-[...]
#tr.en: May holy @wDN{An} sit with the shepherd!
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; An[1]DN; kug[pure]; X
#etcsl: line-id=50

51. sipad {d}ur-{d}namma-da saŋ [...]
#tr.en: …… with the shepherd @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}.
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; Urnamma[1]RN; saŋ[head]; X
#etcsl: line-id=51

@div trailer 

52. šir₃-nam-šub {d}nanna-kam!#
#tr.en: A @fsux{šir-namšub} of @wDN{Nanna}.
#lem: širnamšubak[subscript]; Nanna[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=52

@end trailer







